1
00:01:47,519 --> 00:01:49,079
Brother Cai, your car is ready.

2
00:01:49,079 --> 00:01:49,760
He's out.

3
00:01:51,560 --> 00:01:52,159
Okay.

4
00:01:57,000 --> 00:01:57,920
Take care, Brother Cai.

5
00:02:32,400 --> 00:02:33,280
In our Second Division,

6
00:02:33,360 --> 00:02:34,680
is Wu Jiali the best driver?

7
00:02:34,680 --> 00:02:35,960
The gray Jetta ahead on the right,

8
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:37,159
the one with the plate ending in 26,

9
00:02:37,520 --> 00:02:38,960
is it tailing Ah Cai's car too?

10
00:02:44,199 --> 00:02:45,199
When did you notice?

11
00:02:45,560 --> 00:02:46,840
When you were born.

12
00:03:16,080 --> 00:03:18,639
A few packs of cigarettes and a bottle of water.

13
00:04:27,240 --> 00:04:28,240
How much gas do you need?

14
00:04:28,519 --> 00:04:29,120
Fill it up.

15
00:04:37,240 --> 00:04:38,160
How much gas for you?

16
00:04:39,920 --> 00:04:40,360
Fill it up.

17
00:04:40,560 --> 00:04:40,959
All right.

18
00:05:03,959 --> 00:05:05,319
Hello, how much gas do you need?

19
00:05:06,319 --> 00:05:06,879
Hello?

20
00:05:07,160 --> 00:05:08,000
How much are you getting?

21
00:05:09,519 --> 00:05:10,519
He didn't pump any gas.

22
00:05:12,199 --> 00:05:13,120
Damn, he's making a run for it!

23
00:05:13,120 --> 00:05:13,879
Quick, pull out the nozzle!

24
00:08:44,559 --> 00:08:45,799
How did you fly up here?

25
00:08:46,000 --> 00:08:48,960
He always rides this motorcycle to the gas station.

26
00:08:48,960 --> 00:08:50,440
Everyone at the gas station knows him.

27
00:08:50,840 --> 00:08:52,360
So they told me he came up the mountain.

28
00:08:58,120 --> 00:08:59,559
Why is it you two again?

29
00:09:00,519 --> 00:09:01,519
What's going on here?

30
00:09:01,519 --> 00:09:02,080
You're just a traffic cop.

31
00:09:02,080 --> 00:09:03,399
Why are you meddling in this?

32
00:09:04,000 --> 00:09:04,840
Take him away.

33
00:09:05,440 --> 00:09:06,279
We're the ones who caught him.

34
00:09:06,279 --> 00:09:07,120
Where are you taking him?

35
00:09:07,120 --> 00:09:08,559
What right do you have to arrest him?

36
00:09:08,960 --> 00:09:10,120
We're taking him with us, no matter what.

37
00:09:11,000 --> 00:09:11,919
We're with State Security.

38
00:09:12,320 --> 00:09:13,200
Let go! Let go!

39
00:09:13,200 --> 00:09:14,000
You're choking me!

40
00:09:17,720 --> 00:09:19,240
We're from the Criminal Investigation Detachment.

41
00:09:19,600 --> 00:09:20,799
He's our suspect.

42
00:09:20,799 --> 00:09:21,919
We've tracked this case for a long time.

43
00:09:25,279 --> 00:09:26,559
How many people did you scam in total?

44
00:09:26,720 --> 00:09:27,679
Where's the rest of the stolen cash?

45
00:09:27,879 --> 00:09:28,799
Where did you hide it?

46
00:09:29,039 --> 00:09:30,120
Who were you supposed to deliver this money to?

47
00:09:30,519 --> 00:09:32,039
And who were you planning to meet today?

48
00:09:33,679 --> 00:09:34,600
Done with the call?

49
00:09:34,600 --> 00:09:35,399
Just wait for word.

50
00:09:35,639 --> 00:09:36,799
Let me tell you this.

51
00:09:37,200 --> 00:09:39,320
The bureau chief has to call my phone personally.

52
00:09:39,879 --> 00:09:41,159
You have a different identity every day.

53
00:09:41,159 --> 00:09:42,200
Who knows what's real and what's fake?

54
00:09:43,080 --> 00:09:43,879
Come on, keep talking.

55
00:09:44,440 --> 00:09:45,159
Look at me.

56
00:09:45,519 --> 00:09:46,879
Did you scam the full amount or just a deposit?

57
00:09:47,120 --> 00:09:48,320
How many phone numbers were there in total?

58
00:09:48,440 --> 00:09:49,639
Who was calling the shots?

59
00:09:49,759 --> 00:09:50,879
You've been caught red-handed.

60
00:09:50,879 --> 00:09:52,120
What's with the silent treatment?

61
00:09:52,360 --> 00:09:53,440
You're in deep trouble, you know that?

62
00:09:53,679 --> 00:09:55,519
Look at me and answer the question.

63
00:09:55,799 --> 00:09:57,039
Answer the question, understand?

64
00:09:57,039 --> 00:09:58,360
You're throwing so many questions at him.

65
00:09:58,879 --> 00:10:00,200
Which one do you expect him to answer?

66
00:10:07,039 --> 00:10:08,399
Start with the first contract.

67
00:10:08,799 --> 00:10:09,919
Gang-related fraud.

68
00:10:10,200 --> 00:10:10,840
Speak up!

69
00:10:10,960 --> 00:10:12,080
I told you to talk!

70
00:10:12,360 --> 00:10:13,600
I need to pee.

71
00:10:14,120 --> 00:10:14,679
Look at that.

72
00:10:14,879 --> 00:10:16,039
You scared him so bad he's about to piss himself.

73
00:10:16,320 --> 00:10:17,840
I told you to go easy on him, but you didn't listen.

74
00:10:19,360 --> 00:10:19,720
Go ahead and pee.

75
00:10:20,279 --> 00:10:21,679
Pee right here so I can see if you actually have to.

76
00:10:35,840 --> 00:10:36,639
I need to take a dump.

77
00:10:45,720 --> 00:10:47,120
Take him to the restroom.

78
00:10:50,960 --> 00:10:52,200
Why are you looking at me?

79
00:10:52,200 --> 00:10:53,559
I need to take notes here.

80
00:10:53,559 --> 00:10:54,440
I wait on you every day.

81
00:10:54,440 --> 00:10:55,960
What's wrong with helping me out today?

82
00:11:02,840 --> 00:11:03,600
Fine.

83
00:11:05,519 --> 00:11:06,279
Let's go.

84
00:11:10,080 --> 00:11:10,879
Go take your dump.

85
00:11:11,679 --> 00:11:12,559
Come here.

86
00:11:12,840 --> 00:11:13,519
Come over and check.

87
00:11:14,039 --> 00:11:15,919
See if the illicit cash I counted is right,

88
00:11:15,919 --> 00:11:17,000
so there's no confusion later.

89
00:11:23,120 --> 00:11:23,720
Li Tang.

90
00:11:24,080 --> 00:11:25,879
I've talked with Director Wu of State Security.

91
00:11:26,080 --> 00:11:27,240
Let State Security interrogate first.

92
00:11:27,399 --> 00:11:28,519
Bring the illicit cash back with you.

93
00:11:28,720 --> 00:11:29,679
Copy that, Director.

94
00:11:29,840 --> 00:11:31,799
All right, we'll leave the cash with you.

95
00:11:31,799 --> 00:11:32,679
We'll head out first.

96
00:12:05,120 --> 00:12:05,840
Baoshan.

97
00:12:06,720 --> 00:12:07,519
Something's up over here.

98
00:12:10,600 --> 00:12:11,080
Xiao Zhang.

99
00:12:11,519 --> 00:12:12,000
Brother Li.

100
00:12:12,080 --> 00:12:12,840
Give that to me.

101
00:12:12,879 --> 00:12:13,279
Here.

102
00:12:14,759 --> 00:12:15,360
Look.

103
00:12:16,159 --> 00:12:17,399
It's all burned paper and documents.

104
00:12:17,399 --> 00:12:18,279
There's even more in the cesspit.

105
00:12:18,679 --> 00:12:19,679
All burned today.

106
00:12:21,039 --> 00:12:22,600
We actually searched the house pretty thoroughly.

107
00:12:22,600 --> 00:12:23,440
Nothing there.

108
00:12:24,159 --> 00:12:24,960
He definitely acted ahead of time,

109
00:12:24,960 --> 00:12:26,279
getting rid of all these things.

110
00:12:26,679 --> 00:12:28,519
Someone tipped him off, for sure.

111
00:12:36,799 --> 00:12:37,279
Brother Qi.

112
00:12:38,120 --> 00:12:39,799
Everything useful in Ah Cai's house

113
00:12:39,799 --> 00:12:40,679
was completely burned.

114
00:12:41,279 --> 00:12:42,000
When we went last time,

115
00:12:42,000 --> 00:12:43,360
he still had government documents at home.

116
00:12:43,360 --> 00:12:44,320
Now they're all gone.

117
00:12:44,320 --> 00:12:45,639
I think he was definitely tipped off.

118
00:12:45,639 --> 00:12:47,840
Or he wouldn't have fled up the mountain.

119
00:12:49,720 --> 00:12:51,600
Back when I handled that case...

120
00:12:52,039 --> 00:12:52,519
Bureau Chief Wei.

121
00:13:53,519 --> 00:13:53,919
Wait,

122
00:13:54,039 --> 00:13:54,879
why are you handcuffing me?

123
00:13:54,879 --> 00:13:55,399
Wu Jiali.

124
00:14:10,519 --> 00:14:11,000
Wait,

125
00:14:11,399 --> 00:14:12,000
Sis Li,

126
00:14:12,519 --> 00:14:13,000
Chief Wei,

127
00:14:13,200 --> 00:14:13,519
what's...

128
00:14:13,519 --> 00:14:14,440
What's going on?

129
00:14:45,600 --> 00:14:48,759
There really is more than one traitor around you.

130
00:14:49,720 --> 00:14:51,720
One of them is buried deep.

131
00:14:52,320 --> 00:14:53,679
All I can tell you is,

132
00:14:54,120 --> 00:14:56,799
this person has deep ties to you.

133
00:15:08,519 --> 00:15:09,399
Done reading?

134
00:15:11,440 --> 00:15:12,440
If you're done, I'll take it back.

135
00:15:57,039 --> 00:15:58,679
Are you two heading out together?

136
00:16:01,600 --> 00:16:02,360
I'm going out alone.

137
00:16:02,639 --> 00:16:03,240
Got something to do?

138
00:16:03,519 --> 00:16:04,080
Yeah.

139
00:16:04,360 --> 00:16:05,159
It's been approved.

140
00:16:05,279 --> 00:16:06,080
In three days,

141
00:16:06,080 --> 00:16:07,440
you'll be transferred to Task Force Two.

142
00:16:07,799 --> 00:16:08,919
Your office stays the same.

143
00:16:11,360 --> 00:16:12,159
Leave it on my desk.

144
00:16:17,320 --> 00:16:18,120
Did you hear me?

145
00:16:18,519 --> 00:16:19,519
Still got three days left.

146
00:16:19,840 --> 00:16:21,000
Three days still makes us partners.

147
00:16:21,360 --> 00:16:22,440
Don't let Brother Qi down.

148
00:16:22,840 --> 00:16:23,720
Don't just stand there.

149
00:16:24,279 --> 00:16:24,919
Go on.

150
00:16:47,320 --> 00:16:48,159
Please,

151
00:16:49,679 --> 00:16:51,200
pass a message to my cousin:

152
00:16:51,799 --> 00:16:53,440
ask her to take good care of the old man.

153
00:16:54,120 --> 00:16:55,200
Her efforts won't be for nothing.

154
00:16:55,600 --> 00:16:58,559
We can transfer the old house to her.

155
00:16:59,639 --> 00:17:01,679
In the bag I carry every day,

156
00:17:02,120 --> 00:17:04,440
are my daily medications.

157
00:17:05,079 --> 00:17:06,200
And also,

158
00:17:07,039 --> 00:17:08,920
a comb and a toothbrush.

159
00:17:09,079 --> 00:17:11,119
Things you take to prison.

160
00:17:17,519 --> 00:17:20,319
Every day has been utter torment.

161
00:17:22,279 --> 00:17:23,920
I've long been prepared for this.

162
00:17:25,200 --> 00:17:26,559
I just didn't know

163
00:17:27,880 --> 00:17:29,319
when this day would come.

164
00:17:31,799 --> 00:17:33,640
I couldn't eat or sleep.

165
00:17:36,119 --> 00:17:38,119
Countless times, I thought of turning myself in.

166
00:17:39,680 --> 00:17:40,640
But whenever I went home

167
00:17:41,319 --> 00:17:43,559
and saw all the endless mess at home,

168
00:17:43,960 --> 00:17:45,160
I lost my nerve again.

169
00:17:45,759 --> 00:17:46,799
I even thought of

170
00:17:46,799 --> 00:17:48,640
ending it all just to be free.

171
00:17:48,920 --> 00:17:50,920
But if I were gone, too,

172
00:17:53,640 --> 00:17:55,160
the young and old of the family...

173
00:17:55,640 --> 00:17:57,000
what would happen to them?

174
00:17:58,920 --> 00:18:01,440
Director Wu, you know

175
00:18:01,640 --> 00:18:04,000
I was given away as a child.

176
00:18:04,519 --> 00:18:05,400
My uncle,

177
00:18:06,640 --> 00:18:07,759
who's now my father,

178
00:18:08,759 --> 00:18:10,039
was really good to me.

179
00:18:11,519 --> 00:18:12,519
He put me through school

180
00:18:13,559 --> 00:18:15,440
and raised me alongside his son.

181
00:18:15,759 --> 00:18:17,039
It was so hard on him.

182
00:18:18,200 --> 00:18:20,640
And I never gave him much of a good life.

183
00:18:20,799 --> 00:18:22,200
But that son of his...

184
00:18:23,519 --> 00:18:25,440
I don't know when he started gambling.

185
00:18:26,799 --> 00:18:27,720
Those people

186
00:18:27,960 --> 00:18:28,599
took the chance

187
00:18:29,000 --> 00:18:30,799
to run him into massive debt.

188
00:18:31,880 --> 00:18:33,079
I couldn't pay it off,

189
00:18:34,839 --> 00:18:36,519
so they had him thrown into prison.

190
00:18:37,079 --> 00:18:38,200
Step by step...

191
00:18:40,200 --> 00:18:41,839
The old man suffered a brain hemorrhage.

192
00:18:42,880 --> 00:18:44,000
Director Wu, back then,

193
00:18:44,240 --> 00:18:46,279
you were the one who found the surgeon,

194
00:18:47,079 --> 00:18:47,920
right?

195
00:18:48,240 --> 00:18:49,880
His life was saved, at least,

196
00:18:52,720 --> 00:18:54,359
but his legs were paralyzed.

197
00:19:12,559 --> 00:19:13,319
Then,

198
00:19:15,880 --> 00:19:16,680
they

199
00:19:18,319 --> 00:19:19,599
paid off my brother's debts,

200
00:19:20,599 --> 00:19:21,839
promised to get his sentence reduced,

201
00:19:22,200 --> 00:19:24,440
provided imported medicine for the old man,

202
00:19:24,759 --> 00:19:26,440
and said whatever complications he had,

203
00:19:26,440 --> 00:19:27,720
the medicine could cure them.

204
00:19:27,720 --> 00:19:29,960
At worst, surgery in Taiwan, China.

205
00:19:29,960 --> 00:19:31,440
and get my uncle back on his feet.

206
00:19:31,880 --> 00:19:33,359
Of course I didn't believe them.

207
00:19:34,720 --> 00:19:35,960
But if I didn't,

208
00:19:36,200 --> 00:19:37,519
they would keep

209
00:19:38,200 --> 00:19:40,000
causing trouble for my family.

210
00:19:42,200 --> 00:19:43,039
So I...

211
00:19:46,039 --> 00:19:47,799
I couldn't refuse.

212
00:19:48,559 --> 00:19:50,119
They knew my weakness.

213
00:19:51,359 --> 00:19:52,119
I was scared.

214
00:20:07,119 --> 00:20:08,319
Your father...

215
00:20:08,799 --> 00:20:10,119
how are the hospital arrangements going?

216
00:20:10,519 --> 00:20:11,160
All set.

217
00:20:15,799 --> 00:20:16,839
It's really strange, though.

218
00:20:20,640 --> 00:20:22,240
I have no idea how he fell.

219
00:20:25,240 --> 00:20:26,039
Yue,

220
00:20:29,319 --> 00:20:31,039
could you maybe...

221
00:20:39,640 --> 00:20:40,279
That's enough.

222
00:20:40,680 --> 00:20:42,160
There's no need for words between us.

223
00:20:42,759 --> 00:20:43,680
Take this and use it for now.

224
00:21:10,119 --> 00:21:11,839
You don't have to do much.

225
00:21:12,519 --> 00:21:15,200
Just nod or shake your head.

226
00:21:18,920 --> 00:21:20,400
Even if he's not your real brother,

227
00:21:21,720 --> 00:21:22,880
you wouldn't want

228
00:21:23,880 --> 00:21:25,200
him to just disappear, would you?

229
00:21:26,839 --> 00:21:27,440
Afterwards,

230
00:21:28,359 --> 00:21:30,519
I didn't dare meet that childhood friend.

231
00:21:31,160 --> 00:21:32,039
Then,

232
00:21:32,920 --> 00:21:34,839
they started following my son.

233
00:21:35,680 --> 00:21:37,920
You didn't reply to my messages.

234
00:21:37,920 --> 00:21:39,519
If I didn't play rough,

235
00:21:39,960 --> 00:21:41,440
I wouldn't have been able to see you.

236
00:21:43,200 --> 00:21:46,680
I didn't ask you to breach discipline.

237
00:21:47,200 --> 00:21:50,000
Just nod or shake your head.

238
00:21:50,319 --> 00:21:51,559
It's not that hard, is it?

239
00:21:53,160 --> 00:21:54,519
You've always cared about family,

240
00:21:54,759 --> 00:21:55,759
always so responsible.

241
00:21:55,759 --> 00:21:57,039
You wouldn't want

242
00:21:57,720 --> 00:21:58,839
anything to happen

243
00:21:59,400 --> 00:22:00,640
to your whole family, would you?

244
00:22:02,680 --> 00:22:04,359
Maozai, the day before yesterday,

245
00:22:04,839 --> 00:22:07,160
went into the internet cafe at 6:35,

246
00:22:07,640 --> 00:22:10,160
and got home at 8:46.

247
00:22:10,640 --> 00:22:11,920
Yesterday,

248
00:22:11,920 --> 00:22:15,839
he got home at 9:22.

249
00:22:20,119 --> 00:22:21,640
I don't know why.

250
00:22:23,279 --> 00:22:24,519
Just a momentary lapse of reason.

251
00:22:25,960 --> 00:22:27,279
Back then, it felt like

252
00:22:28,319 --> 00:22:30,160
I wasn't even myself anymore.

253
00:22:31,039 --> 00:22:32,599
My conscience couldn't take it.

254
00:22:33,279 --> 00:22:34,960
So many times I wanted to turn myself in.

255
00:22:35,519 --> 00:22:36,359
Several times,

256
00:22:37,079 --> 00:22:38,880
I was standing right outside your door,

257
00:22:39,640 --> 00:22:41,519
my hand already raised.

258
00:22:42,000 --> 00:22:42,920
But every time,

259
00:22:43,400 --> 00:22:45,240
that voice of false hope cropped up,

260
00:22:45,920 --> 00:22:47,519
grabbing me by the throat,

261
00:22:47,519 --> 00:22:48,880
forcing me to back down.

262
00:22:49,839 --> 00:22:50,720
And just like that,

263
00:22:51,839 --> 00:22:52,880
I didn't dare look back,

264
00:22:53,640 --> 00:22:55,079
let alone look ahead.

265
00:22:55,759 --> 00:22:57,000
I couldn't escape them,

266
00:22:58,079 --> 00:22:59,799
so I could only force myself to be numb,

267
00:23:00,160 --> 00:23:02,839
living like a walking corpse.

268
00:23:03,680 --> 00:23:04,799
I regret it so much.

269
00:23:05,759 --> 00:23:06,519
One wrong step,

270
00:23:07,519 --> 00:23:08,319
and every step went wrong.

271
00:23:08,960 --> 00:23:10,519
I could never break free.

272
00:23:11,519 --> 00:23:12,200
A few days ago,

273
00:23:13,200 --> 00:23:15,119
she suddenly called me again.

274
00:23:15,720 --> 00:23:17,240
"If there's an operation soon,

275
00:23:17,240 --> 00:23:18,599
remember our deal."

276
00:23:23,000 --> 00:23:23,680
I'm sorry.

277
00:23:25,039 --> 00:23:25,759
I'm sorry.

278
00:23:28,599 --> 00:23:29,680
I'm so sorry.

279
00:23:30,079 --> 00:23:31,200
I let the organization down,

280
00:23:32,119 --> 00:23:33,200
I let all of you down,

281
00:23:33,759 --> 00:23:34,720
and the Second Division,

282
00:23:35,559 --> 00:23:37,079
the Comrades I worked with every day.

283
00:23:37,519 --> 00:23:39,720
I am overwhelmed with guilt.

284
00:23:40,519 --> 00:23:42,000
I wanted to change things too,

285
00:23:42,519 --> 00:23:43,759
but I really...

286
00:23:43,759 --> 00:23:46,240
I really couldn't find a way out.

287
00:23:46,880 --> 00:23:49,119
I was losing my mind!

288
00:23:51,839 --> 00:23:53,240
I could only act like

289
00:23:54,599 --> 00:23:56,240
a spineless ostrich,

290
00:23:59,519 --> 00:24:00,240
manipulated by them...

291
00:24:04,599 --> 00:24:05,839
It's all my fault.

292
00:24:06,519 --> 00:24:07,519
It's all my fault.

293
00:24:09,279 --> 00:24:10,160
It's all my fault.

294
00:24:12,920 --> 00:24:14,079
It's all my fault.

295
00:24:14,720 --> 00:24:16,079
We've been watching you for two years.

296
00:24:17,279 --> 00:24:18,079
This time was

297
00:24:18,400 --> 00:24:19,359
the third test.

298
00:24:20,079 --> 00:24:21,440
For today's arrest operation,

299
00:24:21,960 --> 00:24:22,960
you were the only one

300
00:24:23,240 --> 00:24:25,039
who was told one hour in advance.

301
00:24:25,759 --> 00:24:26,559
The message...

302
00:24:28,200 --> 00:24:29,440
you leaked it to them,

303
00:24:30,359 --> 00:24:30,960
didn't you?

304
00:24:33,519 --> 00:24:34,559
"Operation is starting."

305
00:24:35,200 --> 00:24:35,880
"Understood."

306
00:24:41,400 --> 00:24:42,079
Yes.

307
00:24:43,160 --> 00:24:44,519
Does Jin Lina know about you two?

308
00:24:46,559 --> 00:24:47,559
No.

309
00:24:47,799 --> 00:24:48,920
She doesn't know a thing.

310
00:24:49,400 --> 00:24:49,960
And the other side

311
00:24:51,039 --> 00:24:53,160
doesn't know our ties to Jin Lina either.

312
00:24:53,640 --> 00:24:54,960
I only agreed

313
00:24:57,599 --> 00:24:59,039
to tip them off.

314
00:24:59,240 --> 00:25:01,960
But I never once betrayed my Comrades.

315
00:25:02,599 --> 00:25:03,839
Chunxiao, Ma Qi,

316
00:25:03,839 --> 00:25:05,039
watching Lin Kanshan,

317
00:25:05,200 --> 00:25:06,680
including what Jinlan is doing right now...

318
00:25:06,680 --> 00:25:07,880
All of that,

319
00:25:08,839 --> 00:25:09,960
I would never say a word.

320
00:25:10,279 --> 00:25:12,319
That was the line I drew for myself.

321
00:25:13,079 --> 00:25:13,720
In Beijing,

322
00:25:14,160 --> 00:25:15,640
you were assigned to monitor Cao Liaoping,

323
00:25:15,880 --> 00:25:17,880
but you were actually providing cover for him.

324
00:25:18,920 --> 00:25:19,680
Isn't that right?

325
00:25:29,759 --> 00:25:30,240
Sis Li.

326
00:25:30,519 --> 00:25:31,000
Where is she?

327
00:25:32,359 --> 00:25:33,039
Haven't seen her.

328
00:25:33,599 --> 00:25:34,960
Might be in the room.

329
00:25:35,839 --> 00:25:36,279
Go check.

330
00:25:36,279 --> 00:25:36,720
Okay.

331
00:27:30,640 --> 00:27:31,440
The way I see it,

332
00:27:31,839 --> 00:27:33,799
only those who've handled real cases,

333
00:27:34,079 --> 00:27:36,279
section chiefs or deputy division heads at least,

334
00:27:36,279 --> 00:27:37,960
actually get any value out of training.

335
00:27:38,400 --> 00:27:40,519
For blank slates like you, it's pointless.

336
00:27:40,839 --> 00:27:43,160
Even the darkest paper was once a blank slate.

337
00:27:43,160 --> 00:27:44,400
You always look down on rookies.

338
00:27:44,400 --> 00:27:45,400
Where else would experience come from?

339
00:27:45,400 --> 00:27:47,279
Doesn't it come from interrogations?

340
00:27:47,279 --> 00:27:48,039
Wrong.

341
00:27:49,000 --> 00:27:50,240
Three types take the interrogation stand.

342
00:27:50,240 --> 00:27:51,640
First is raw talent.

343
00:27:51,640 --> 00:27:53,039
Some people are just born for this.

344
00:27:53,039 --> 00:27:54,240
Maybe one in ten.

345
00:27:54,240 --> 00:27:55,599
Asset turning, major cases, snap queries—

346
00:27:55,599 --> 00:27:56,559
they can crack them all.

347
00:27:56,559 --> 00:27:58,160
When it goes well, it takes under three days.

348
00:27:58,160 --> 00:27:59,319
That's a genius.

349
00:27:59,319 --> 00:28:00,759
The second kind is the capable.

350
00:28:00,759 --> 00:28:01,960
Sharp instincts, quick mind.

351
00:28:01,960 --> 00:28:03,279
Starting with minor cases and moving up,

352
00:28:03,519 --> 00:28:05,000
with proper training, they can excel.

353
00:28:05,000 --> 00:28:06,440
The third kind is hopeless.

354
00:28:06,440 --> 00:28:07,400
Plain mediocrities.

355
00:28:07,400 --> 00:28:08,960
They just aren't cut out for interrogation.

356
00:28:08,960 --> 00:28:10,079
Like you.

357
00:28:10,079 --> 00:28:11,000
As for Huadong,

358
00:28:11,000 --> 00:28:12,039
he barely makes the second category.

359
00:28:12,039 --> 00:28:13,039
Jinlan has promise.

360
00:28:13,039 --> 00:28:14,839
She has potential, but isn't a genius.

361
00:28:15,039 --> 00:28:16,079
Then who is a genius?

362
00:28:18,279 --> 00:28:19,880
Those who don't ask foolish questions.

363
00:28:39,799 --> 00:28:41,599
The fatalities from his demolition work—

364
00:28:41,599 --> 00:28:42,359
are they confirmed?

365
00:28:42,359 --> 00:28:43,240
One dead and two injured.

366
00:28:43,240 --> 00:28:44,599
When the victim's family petitioned,

367
00:28:44,599 --> 00:28:46,039
they were beaten into disability.

368
00:28:46,039 --> 00:28:47,319
He did it with his own hands.

369
00:28:48,519 --> 00:28:49,279
What else?

370
00:28:49,279 --> 00:28:51,000
It seems the MIB used his projects

371
00:28:51,000 --> 00:28:52,279
to funnel funds in.

372
00:28:52,279 --> 00:28:54,400
The specific intel details are unclear.

373
00:28:54,400 --> 00:28:55,519
Better get that out of him today.

374
00:28:55,960 --> 00:28:57,119
Why is he a vegetarian?

375
00:28:57,119 --> 00:28:58,599
Faith, or something else?

376
00:28:58,599 --> 00:28:59,839
Not really sure about that.

377
00:29:00,559 --> 00:29:01,400
Let's get ready to start.

378
00:29:03,880 --> 00:29:04,920
Anything else to add?

379
00:29:05,839 --> 00:29:07,160
I asked you before:

380
00:29:07,160 --> 00:29:09,279
Who's a genius in the interrogation room?

381
00:29:09,759 --> 00:29:10,319
Have you ever seen one?

382
00:29:11,400 --> 00:29:12,279
There are no geniuses.

383
00:29:12,920 --> 00:29:13,920
Everyone's just ordinary.

384
00:29:16,000 --> 00:29:17,279
You wanted to put up buildings,

385
00:29:17,440 --> 00:29:18,519
so you tore down the homes

386
00:29:18,519 --> 00:29:20,799
folks lived in for half their lives.

387
00:29:20,799 --> 00:29:22,400
Not a single tile left within three days,

388
00:29:22,400 --> 00:29:23,839
or else you'd play rough.

389
00:29:24,000 --> 00:29:25,759
You also preyed on the real estate craze,

390
00:29:25,759 --> 00:29:27,160
using high returns as bait

391
00:29:27,240 --> 00:29:29,359
to lure investors into your fake projects.

392
00:29:29,440 --> 00:29:31,279
In truth, those investment projects of yours,

393
00:29:31,400 --> 00:29:32,279
from start to finish,

394
00:29:32,279 --> 00:29:34,039
only existed in promotional brochures.

395
00:29:34,039 --> 00:29:35,319
Ground was never going to be broken.

396
00:29:35,319 --> 00:29:37,519
You bled those investors dry.

397
00:29:37,519 --> 00:29:38,920
Resorting to such dirty tricks,

398
00:29:39,160 --> 00:29:40,200
aren't you afraid of going to hell?

399
00:29:40,680 --> 00:29:42,519
Does your religious mother

400
00:29:42,799 --> 00:29:43,799
know anything about this?

401
00:29:48,960 --> 00:29:51,839
I hear you pray to gods before going out.

402
00:29:52,519 --> 00:29:53,920
How are you going to explain yourself to them?

403
00:29:54,200 --> 00:29:56,319
When the evictees organized a meeting,

404
00:29:56,319 --> 00:29:58,519
you turned informants and set up wiretaps.

405
00:29:58,799 --> 00:30:00,559
Where did you get that surveillance gear?

406
00:30:01,720 --> 00:30:03,519
Did the MIB give it to you, or sell it to you?

407
00:30:03,759 --> 00:30:05,720
After the hard tactics, you played soft.

408
00:30:06,160 --> 00:30:07,759
You put a stack of cash on the table,

409
00:30:07,759 --> 00:30:09,119
and right beside it,

410
00:30:09,119 --> 00:30:10,519
a freshly severed, bloody finger.

411
00:30:10,519 --> 00:30:12,680
Whoever agreed to move took the cash right then.

412
00:30:12,799 --> 00:30:14,400
You took all that freshly collected cash

413
00:30:14,400 --> 00:30:15,880
and poured it into your own projects.

414
00:30:15,880 --> 00:30:17,599
Isn't the MIB after you for their money?

415
00:30:24,759 --> 00:30:26,240
Maybe the big boss is hungry,

416
00:30:26,240 --> 00:30:27,440
too weak to speak.

417
00:30:27,440 --> 00:30:28,319
Let's eat then.

418
00:31:10,079 --> 00:31:12,000
Actually, it's all just business.

419
00:31:12,519 --> 00:31:14,160
You can deal with the MIB,

420
00:31:14,519 --> 00:31:15,799
so we can make a deal too.

421
00:31:15,960 --> 00:31:17,839
It comes down to the bargaining chips.

422
00:31:18,440 --> 00:31:19,599
Let's not talk about the case today.

423
00:31:19,599 --> 00:31:20,799
We can talk business instead.

424
00:31:21,000 --> 00:31:22,680
What you want, what I want...

425
00:31:22,680 --> 00:31:24,119
Let's see how we can make a trade.

426
00:31:24,119 --> 00:31:25,160
Think it over first.

427
00:31:37,720 --> 00:31:39,400
Right now, you're just a bug in a bowl.

428
00:31:40,559 --> 00:31:42,559
Whether to pour in hot water or hot oil...

429
00:31:42,880 --> 00:31:44,200
...is my call.

430
00:31:44,599 --> 00:31:46,240
But you can also choose to crawl out,

431
00:31:46,599 --> 00:31:47,359
or...

432
00:31:47,559 --> 00:31:48,599
...suffer a little less.

433
00:31:58,160 --> 00:31:59,519
The reprimand has nothing to do with you.

434
00:31:59,519 --> 00:32:01,000
Planting the bug was my call originally.

435
00:32:01,000 --> 00:32:01,920
You had no idea anyway.

436
00:32:02,799 --> 00:32:04,160
He won't take the hard approach,

437
00:32:04,160 --> 00:32:05,799
nor the soft one.

438
00:32:05,799 --> 00:32:08,119
Even dirty tricks seem useless on him.

439
00:32:08,599 --> 00:32:09,799
He's a wily old fox.

440
00:32:09,920 --> 00:32:11,519
If not today, then tomorrow.

441
00:32:11,519 --> 00:32:12,519
Just wear him down slowly.

442
00:32:12,519 --> 00:32:14,000
How long is that going to take?

443
00:32:14,000 --> 00:32:14,839
The day after tomorrow.

444
00:32:15,279 --> 00:32:17,119
Until I'm on another task force.

445
00:32:17,119 --> 00:32:18,640
Then I won't have to deal with this mess.

446
00:32:25,079 --> 00:32:26,200
How did you get sick too?

447
00:32:26,960 --> 00:32:28,519
From staying up late, or what?

448
00:32:30,240 --> 00:32:31,440
An endocrine issue.

449
00:32:34,079 --> 00:32:35,160
Then go get tested first.

450
00:32:35,160 --> 00:32:36,000
I'll head over as soon as I can.

451
00:32:36,640 --> 00:32:37,519
Got it.

452
00:32:39,759 --> 00:32:41,079
If you need any help,

453
00:32:41,079 --> 00:32:42,519
running errands, picking up meds,

454
00:32:42,519 --> 00:32:43,559
I'm available.

455
00:32:44,000 --> 00:32:45,640
Life is like having a meal.

456
00:32:45,640 --> 00:32:47,039
You eat yours, and I'll eat mine.

457
00:32:47,039 --> 00:32:48,440
Everyone has their own troubles.

458
00:32:49,160 --> 00:32:50,759
There are things you just can't help with.

459
00:32:53,240 --> 00:32:53,839
I'm off.

460
00:33:34,359 --> 00:33:36,039
Why can't we pay what's due?

461
00:33:36,640 --> 00:33:38,960
Funds and headcount were approved earlier.

462
00:33:38,960 --> 00:33:40,119
Why change it?

463
00:33:41,039 --> 00:33:41,960
Don't beat around the bush with me.

464
00:33:41,960 --> 00:33:44,359
Just tell me whose call this was.

465
00:33:50,920 --> 00:33:52,559
The superiors have their reasons, sure,

466
00:33:53,839 --> 00:33:56,559
but you have to let me know in time.

467
00:33:56,559 --> 00:33:58,039
Otherwise, how do I explain this to them?

468
00:33:58,279 --> 00:34:00,640
They'll think we're an amateur outfit.

469
00:34:00,799 --> 00:34:02,759
If you worked without getting paid,

470
00:34:02,799 --> 00:34:03,759
how would you feel?

471
00:34:20,840 --> 00:34:21,639
Secretary Niu,

472
00:34:22,679 --> 00:34:23,519
it's Old Zhu.

473
00:34:24,039 --> 00:34:25,880
It's about the funding.

474
00:34:26,719 --> 00:34:29,920
I worked so hard to get a mainland asset,

475
00:34:30,519 --> 00:34:32,199
from the State Security Bureau, no less.

476
00:34:32,199 --> 00:34:33,840
The terms promised to him

477
00:34:33,840 --> 00:34:35,519
aren't being honored at all.

478
00:34:35,719 --> 00:34:36,920
I have zero credibility left.

479
00:34:36,920 --> 00:34:37,559
What am I supposed to do?

480
00:34:38,039 --> 00:34:40,360
My own reputation doesn't matter,

481
00:34:40,639 --> 00:34:43,119
but the MIB's dignity is on the line.

482
00:34:43,519 --> 00:34:46,280
In intel operations, every penny counts.

483
00:34:46,280 --> 00:34:47,159
You came up from field operations.

484
00:34:47,159 --> 00:34:48,239
You know how this works.

485
00:34:49,719 --> 00:34:50,719
That's why

486
00:34:51,199 --> 00:34:53,239
I'm begging you to help me out.

487
00:34:53,239 --> 00:34:54,800
You're my buffer.

488
00:34:55,159 --> 00:34:57,719
You can at least soften the blow for me.

489
00:34:58,000 --> 00:35:00,519
What if I ask directly and get shut down?

490
00:35:00,679 --> 00:35:01,519
And another thing,

491
00:35:02,719 --> 00:35:06,159
The HK unit's deputy liaison post is open.

492
00:35:06,159 --> 00:35:07,719
I've been keeping an eye on it for you.

493
00:35:08,119 --> 00:35:09,559
This isn't a trade-off, of course.

494
00:35:11,800 --> 00:35:13,159
All right, all right.

495
00:35:13,920 --> 00:35:14,719
Okay.

496
00:35:14,719 --> 00:35:15,559
I'm counting on you.

497
00:35:19,920 --> 00:35:20,800
Do they think

498
00:35:20,800 --> 00:35:22,199
I've gone senile?

499
00:35:22,840 --> 00:35:24,599
He brought in someone from State Security

500
00:35:24,800 --> 00:35:26,079
to give us intel,

501
00:35:26,239 --> 00:35:28,159
yet he refuses to betray his own people,

502
00:35:29,400 --> 00:35:31,719
hasn't delivered any major intelligence,

503
00:35:31,920 --> 00:35:33,199
and only asks for money.

504
00:35:33,400 --> 00:35:35,119
When I play mahjong, I want the whole pot!

505
00:35:36,039 --> 00:35:37,559
What good is a chicken hand?

506
00:35:37,840 --> 00:35:39,760
What's the use of petty gains?

507
00:35:39,960 --> 00:35:43,000
Padding the numbers with small fry...

508
00:35:43,639 --> 00:35:45,679
Is he playing me, or being played?

509
00:35:45,880 --> 00:35:47,119
Fair exchange—

510
00:35:48,119 --> 00:35:49,880
even a child understands that.

511
00:35:50,280 --> 00:35:51,320
Old Zhu,

512
00:35:51,599 --> 00:35:53,079
he's the one who's gone senile.

513
00:36:50,239 --> 00:36:52,800
I got buns and eggs from the cafeteria,

514
00:36:53,159 --> 00:36:54,519
and dropped them off at your place.

515
00:36:57,679 --> 00:37:00,119
I've briefed your sister on everything.

516
00:37:03,800 --> 00:37:05,760
I was going to bring seaweed soup too,

517
00:37:06,119 --> 00:37:07,519
but I was in such a rush

518
00:37:07,840 --> 00:37:09,079
that I dropped it and it spilled.

519
00:37:21,599 --> 00:37:22,440
Thank...

520
00:37:22,800 --> 00:37:23,599
Thank you.

521
00:37:29,639 --> 00:37:31,079
A lightbulb at home went out,

522
00:37:31,079 --> 00:37:32,360
and they said they couldn't get it fixed.

523
00:37:32,519 --> 00:37:33,840
It was actually an issue with the wiring.

524
00:37:34,199 --> 00:37:35,840
I had someone from logistics replace it.

525
00:37:35,840 --> 00:37:38,239
The water and power will be checked again.

526
00:37:38,599 --> 00:37:40,239
The gas stove is also being replaced.

527
00:37:40,239 --> 00:37:41,239
All these things...

528
00:37:42,840 --> 00:37:44,199
I'll keep checking in on them from now on.

529
00:37:49,360 --> 00:37:50,599
I told your sister

530
00:37:50,960 --> 00:37:53,079
if anything happens to your dad or kids,

531
00:37:53,079 --> 00:37:54,320
to call me anytime.

532
00:37:56,599 --> 00:37:57,840
I promised Third Brother

533
00:37:58,920 --> 00:38:00,039
that as long as I'm alive,

534
00:38:00,840 --> 00:38:02,239
I'll look after the whole family to the end.

535
00:38:13,199 --> 00:38:14,519
When Jiang Zaizhen died,

536
00:38:14,519 --> 00:38:15,760
I knew there was a mole among us.

537
00:38:15,760 --> 00:38:17,280
Right in that office.

538
00:38:17,280 --> 00:38:18,880
I didn't know who it was.

539
00:38:18,880 --> 00:38:20,360
I went through everyone one by one.

540
00:38:20,360 --> 00:38:21,760
Every time I thought of you,

541
00:38:21,760 --> 00:38:23,400
I'd skip past it in my mind.

542
00:38:23,400 --> 00:38:24,920
I was terrified it might be you.

543
00:38:24,920 --> 00:38:26,559
What if it really was you?

544
00:38:27,840 --> 00:38:29,199
What about your son?

545
00:38:29,199 --> 00:38:30,880
What about your whole family?

546
00:38:32,079 --> 00:38:33,320
I didn't even dare to imagine.

547
00:38:34,519 --> 00:38:35,960
Why did you do this?

548
00:38:36,639 --> 00:38:38,320
I offered you money every month,

549
00:38:38,320 --> 00:38:39,320
but you wouldn't take it.

550
00:38:39,840 --> 00:38:40,559
If it wasn't enough,

551
00:38:40,559 --> 00:38:42,159
you should've told me. Just say the word!

552
00:38:42,679 --> 00:38:43,679
Even when I bought a TV for your home,

553
00:38:43,679 --> 00:38:44,599
you returned it.

554
00:38:44,599 --> 00:38:45,679
You never said what you were missing.

555
00:38:45,679 --> 00:38:46,360
You wouldn't take mine,

556
00:38:46,360 --> 00:38:47,639
yet you took money from the MIB.

557
00:38:51,400 --> 00:38:52,199
Yes,

558
00:38:54,039 --> 00:38:55,440
what happened to Third Brother was on me.

559
00:38:55,440 --> 00:38:56,039
It was my mistake.

560
00:38:56,039 --> 00:38:58,000
Blame me, hate me, it doesn't matter.

561
00:38:58,000 --> 00:38:59,599
But why throw your own life away?

562
00:38:59,599 --> 00:39:00,639
How could you be so foolish?

563
00:39:07,840 --> 00:39:09,079
When I burn paper offerings,

564
00:39:10,039 --> 00:39:11,920
what am I supposed to tell Third Brother?

565
00:39:13,519 --> 00:39:15,760
He'll feel he died abroad for nothing,

566
00:39:15,760 --> 00:39:16,800
sacrificed in vain.

567
00:39:23,360 --> 00:39:24,440
I told you long ago,

568
00:39:24,440 --> 00:39:26,639
you're not cut out for intelligence work.

569
00:39:26,639 --> 00:39:27,400
Born to be a shield,

570
00:39:27,400 --> 00:39:28,199
yet you insisted on being a spear.

571
00:39:28,199 --> 00:39:29,880
Forcing down what you couldn't swallow.

572
00:39:29,880 --> 00:39:30,800
Go on, choke it down!

573
00:39:31,000 --> 00:39:32,239
And now you're bursting from it.

574
00:39:54,360 --> 00:39:55,119
It's all...

575
00:40:00,719 --> 00:40:01,840
It's all fate, I guess.

576
00:40:06,840 --> 00:40:08,440
I've thought about it, too.

577
00:40:11,159 --> 00:40:12,519
What if, back then,

578
00:40:14,719 --> 00:40:16,119
I hadn't left the service?

579
00:40:16,119 --> 00:40:17,639
What if, when assigned,

580
00:40:17,639 --> 00:40:18,880
I'd been sent to another division?

581
00:40:19,320 --> 00:40:20,320
What if, back then,

582
00:40:21,639 --> 00:40:23,280
I hadn't married Old Li?

583
00:40:24,679 --> 00:40:25,280
And he...

584
00:40:28,679 --> 00:40:30,239
hadn't been your partner?

585
00:40:31,960 --> 00:40:32,559
And...

586
00:40:40,440 --> 00:40:41,239
what if,

587
00:40:42,559 --> 00:40:43,559
when those from Taiwan, China set me up,

588
00:40:43,559 --> 00:40:45,760
I had never gone along with it?

589
00:40:47,079 --> 00:40:48,119
Then now...

590
00:40:51,119 --> 00:40:52,239
things right now...

591
00:40:54,320 --> 00:40:55,519
would definitely be different.

592
00:40:57,320 --> 00:40:58,519
But in life,

593
00:40:59,599 --> 00:41:01,079
there aren't that many what-ifs.

594
00:41:09,639 --> 00:41:10,719
No matter how much you regret it,

595
00:41:13,719 --> 00:41:16,320
you'll never get a second chance.

596
00:41:25,360 --> 00:41:26,400
Let's leave it at that.

597
00:41:33,440 --> 00:41:34,519
Just leave it at that.

598
00:41:36,719 --> 00:41:37,800
You should leave.

599
00:41:40,199 --> 00:41:40,880
Just go.

600
00:42:00,440 --> 00:42:01,159
Xiao Ma,

601
00:42:03,519 --> 00:42:06,280
please tell my son...

602
00:42:09,920 --> 00:42:11,119
just say I'm on a business trip,

603
00:42:12,039 --> 00:42:14,719
to the same place as Old Li.

604
00:42:16,000 --> 00:42:16,760
All right?

605
00:42:22,840 --> 00:42:23,559
I'm begging you.

606
00:43:08,440 --> 00:43:09,519
I'm Wang Kai,

607
00:43:09,519 --> 00:43:11,239
inviting you to watch the drama series

608
00:43:11,239 --> 00:43:12,079
*Confrontation*.

609
00:43:12,639 --> 00:43:14,480
Who you are is none of my business.

610
00:43:14,480 --> 00:43:15,480
You're you, and I'm me.

611
00:43:15,480 --> 00:43:16,480
Don't lump us together.

612
00:43:16,480 --> 00:43:18,119
Never drag me into this again, understand?

613
00:43:18,400 --> 00:43:19,400
All right, all right.

614
00:43:19,400 --> 00:43:20,960
We're doing business together, after all.

615
00:43:20,960 --> 00:43:22,679
I'll send you to the travel agency soon.

616
00:43:22,679 --> 00:43:23,800
What do you need me to do?

617
00:43:23,800 --> 00:43:24,639
Nothing at all.

618
00:43:24,639 --> 00:43:25,639
Cut the act.

619
00:43:25,920 --> 00:43:26,800
Special personnel for special cases.

620
00:43:26,800 --> 00:43:28,639
Once Ah Cai's case is wrapped up,

621
00:43:28,639 --> 00:43:29,760
you can get your transfer,

622
00:43:29,760 --> 00:43:30,559
and take your new post.

623
00:43:30,559 --> 00:43:32,039
The plot where you built the factory

624
00:43:32,039 --> 00:43:33,480
was originally allocated to Lin Kanshan.

625
00:43:33,480 --> 00:43:35,559
Hand the factory and equipment to him.

626
00:43:35,559 --> 00:43:36,960
And what if I refuse?
